+# Governance
+
+WSLCC is a single-maintainer, spare-time open-source project. This document sets expectations so
+contributors know how decisions are made.
+
+## Roles
+
+- **Maintainer** — currently a single person (the project author). Has final say on scope, design,
+  releases, and what gets merged.
+- **Contributors** — anyone who opens issues or pull requests. Very welcome, subject to review.
+
+## Decision making
+
+- Decisions are made by the maintainer, informed by discussion in issues and pull requests.
+- There is no formal voting process. When in doubt, open an issue to discuss before investing in a
+  large change.
+
+## Scope
+
+- The project aims to provide a `docker compose`-style experience for WSL containers, with a unified
+  interface across providers. Features outside that scope may be declined to keep the project
+  maintainable.
+
+## Expectations and cadence
+
+- This is spare-time work: reviews, responses, and releases are best-effort with no SLA.
+- Breaking changes are expected while the project is pre-1.0 and are recorded in
+  [CHANGELOG.md](CHANGELOG.md).
+
+## Continuity
+
+- If maintenance stops, the MIT license permits forking. The project may add additional maintainers
+  over time if sustained, high-quality contributions warrant it.
